  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility using AI algorithms, which initial findings suggest could increase efficiency by 20%. The team has expanded by five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase (celebrated October 10th) and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The project has received a $2M budget approval. Current phases include moving from design to development (led by Omar Jensen) and upcoming user interface enhancements in October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year."
